The key insight is in `tune_quant` at lines 5475-5488. When a quantifier has a string body with exact repetition (e.g., `a{3}`), it converts the quantifier node to a string node and concatenates the body string `n` times. After this, the body is freed.

But wait - this conversion happens during `tune_tree`, which is called BEFORE `set_optimize_info_from_tree` (which calls `optimize_nodes`). So by the time `optimize_nodes` runs, the node is already a `NODE_STRING`, not a `NODE_QUANT`. So `optimize_nodes` should handle it correctly.

